{%- comment -%}
  mm-diamonds — the Diamonds tab's two sub-zones, matched to live 29/08/2026.

  Live structure:

    White Diamonds            | Fancy Coloured
    View all ->               |
    Natural / Lab-Grown       | Natural / Lab-Grown
    Shop by shape - all cuts  | Shop by colour
    [ 6-col cut grid ]        | [ 2-col swatches ]
                              | View all colours ->

  Static, like mm-cuts: a fixed taxonomy with one collection each. A linklist
  would carry the titles and lose the sub-zone structure, the sublink row and
  the swatch colours.

  NOTE on the cut count: live's label reads "all 25 cuts" and renders 25.
  Confirmed against live's own HTML — do not "correct" this to 35.

  Params: none.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* The two sub-zone heads must sit level. White Diamonds carries a View All
     (a 24px icon row); Fancy Coloured does not, so its title floated 24px
     higher. Pin both heads to the same height and bottom-align the contents. */
  .fye .mm-dg-colhead { min-height: 24px; align-items: flex-end; }
</style>
<div class="mm-dg-cols">

  <section class="mm-dg-col">
    <div class="mm-dg-colhead">
      <h3 class="mm-dg-coltitle">White Diamonds</h3>
      <a class="mm-viewall-link" href="/collections/loose-diamonds">
        View all
        {% render 'icon', name: 'arrow-right', size: 13 %}
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="mm-dg-sublinks">
      <a href="/collections/natural-diamonds">Natural</a>
      <a href="/collections/lab-diamonds">Lab-Grown</a>
    </p>
    {%- render 'mm-cuts', label: 'Shop by shape — all 25 cuts' -%}
  </section>

  <section class="mm-dg-col mm-dg-col--aside">
    <div class="mm-dg-colhead">
      <h3 class="mm-dg-coltitle">Fancy Coloured</h3>
    </div>
    <p class="mm-dg-sublinks">
      <a href="/collections/fancy-natural-diamonds">Natural</a>
      <a href="/collections/fancy-lab-grown-diamonds">Lab-Grown</a>
    </p>
    <p class="mm-col-label">Shop by colour</p>
    {%- comment -%}
      Row-major, as live: Yellow/Pink on the first row, then Blue/Green,
      Champagne/Cognac, Grey/Black, Salt &amp; Pepper/Orange. Keep this array
      interleaved — the CSS relies on markup order being reading order.
      Pale swatches take a hairline or they vanish on ivory.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <ul class="mm-dg-swatches mm-dg-swatches--2col">
      <li><a href="/collections/fancy-yellow-diamonds"><span class="mm__dot" style="background:#E3C14E"></span><span>Yellow</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/collections/fancy-pink-diamonds"><span class="mm__dot" style="background:#E88FB0"></span><span>Pink</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/collections/fancy-blue-diamonds"><span class="mm__dot" style="background:#6FA8DC"></span><span>Blue</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/collections/fancy-green-diamonds"><span class="mm__dot" style="background:#7FB77E"></span><span>Green</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/collections/fancy-champagne-diamonds"><span class="mm__dot" style="background:#B99A78"></span><span>Champagne</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/collections/fancy-cognac-diamonds"><span class="mm__dot" style="background:#8A5A3B"></span><span>Cognac</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/collections/fancy-gray-diamonds"><span class="mm__dot" style="background:#A8A8B8"></span><span>Grey</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/collections/black-diamonds"><span class="mm__dot" style="background:#141414"></span><span>Black</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/collections/salt-and-pepper-diamonds"><span class="mm__dot mm__dot--pale" style="background:#F2F1E8"></span><span>Salt &amp; Pepper</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/collections/fancy-orange-diamonds"><span class="mm__dot" style="background:#E0713E"></span><span>Orange</span></a></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="mm-dg-colfoot">
      <a class="mm-viewall-link" href="/collections/fancy-diamonds">
        View all colours
        {% render 'icon', name: 'arrow-right', size: 13 %}
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>
